<div class="key-takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li>The <strong>fire insurance adjuster</strong> your insurer sends, whether staff or independent, works for the insurer. A licensed public adjuster is the only adjuster who works for you.</li>
<li>A fire claim is really several claims: the structure, other structures, contents, additional living expenses, and often smoke, soot, and water from firefighting.</li>
<li>Photograph and inventory everything before cleanup, and do not discard damaged items until they are documented and the insurer has had a chance to see them.</li>
